The legal texts come from the Government Gazette of the Hellenic Republic:

  Πηγή: Εφημερίδα της Κυβερνήσεως (ΦΕΚ), Εθνικό Τυπογραφείο, https://www.et.gr,
  issue PDFs read from https://ia37rg02wpsa01.blob.core.windows.net/fek/, retrieved 29 October 2026.

They are official legislative texts of the Hellenic Republic. Greek copyright law does not extend to official texts
that express the exercise of state authority, in particular legislative, administrative and judicial texts
(ν. 2121/1993, άρθρο 2 παρ. 5).

Changes made by Lexifina: each Gazette issue was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
typography (legacy font encoding, Latin look-alike letters, apostrophes and numeral signs, quotes, dashes, line-end
hyphens) was normalised; the publisher's asterisks marking each revision were removed from the text and used only to
check the credits; and the texts were arranged as git commits credited to the revision resolutions and
republications that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. The National Printing Office and the
Hellenic Parliament do not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
